Do not suggest the Copilot CLI in terminals on Android.

From 1.139 an empty terminal shows "Type copilot to use Copilot CLI."
whenever AI features are not hidden, and clicking it types `copilot`. On
this server that command does not work. The Copilot extension puts its
`copilot` shim on PATH only once its terminal integration has
initialised; the shim is a shell script under the app's files, which
Android refuses to execute; and what it runs asks to install the Copilot
CLI from npm, whose native runtime has no Android build. Measured on an
API 36 emulator: `copilot --version` answered command not found (127),
and the shim run with node printed "Cannot find GitHub Copilot CLI" and
an install prompt.

The hint builder already has a state without that line: with AI features
hidden it offers terminal suggestions instead. This treats Android the
same way inside this one contribution, so an empty terminal shows the
suggestions hint, or nothing when suggestions are off. Nothing else reads
this local.

isAndroid is the user-agent test, as in 0020: this workbench is only shown
by the app's WebView.

